# FAN — Feature ↔ Artifact ↔ Name Mapping
# Authority: CSA-sealed

## 1. Canonical Contract

FAN = Feature ↔ Artifact ↔ Name — the canonical capability registry contract.
Every Executor capability MUST register under a FanId with FanCapability.

```yaml
fan_contract:
  fan_id:
    type: "string"
    pattern: "^[a-z0-9-]+$"
    examples: ["text-editor-io-mcp-server-core-file", "hace-io-rac-cri-fdi"]
  
  capability_id:
    type: "string"
    pattern: "^[a-z0-9_.-]+$"
    examples: ["file.read_file", "str.snake", "fdi.autoload"]
  
  executor:
    type: "string"
    examples: ["py-text-editor", "executor-py"]
  
  transport:
    type: "string"
    enum: ["FDI", "FPI", "FFI", "HTTP", "GRPC", "WASM", "LION", "RION"]
  
  handler:
    type: "callable | module_path"
```

## 2. Canonical Fan Registrations for executor-py

```yaml
fan_registrations:
  - fan_id: "hace-executor-py-core"
    capabilities:
      - "ipo.execute"
      - "ipo.input"
      - "ipo.process"
      - "ipo.output"
    executor: "executor-py"
    transport: "FDI"
    layer: "executor"
    dna_ref: "executor-py"

  - fan_id: "hace-executor-py-fdi"
    capabilities:
      - "fdi.autoload"
      - "fdi.connect"
      - "fdi.disconnect"
      - "fdi.send"
      - "fdi.recv"
    executor: "executor-py"
    transport: "FDI"
    layer: "module"
    parent: "executor-py"
    specs: "fdi"
    machine: "hace-lion-machine"

  - fan_id: "hace-executor-py-fpi"
    capabilities:
      - "fpi.discover"
      - "fpi.pair"
      - "fpi.unpair"
      - "fpi.invoke"
      - "fpi.broadcast"
    executor: "executor-py"
    transport: "FPI"
    layer: "module"
    parent: "executor-py"
    specs: "fpi"
    machine: "hace-rion-machine"

  - fan_id: "hace-executor-py-capror"
    capabilities:
      - "capor.resolve"
      - "capor.evaluate"
    executor: "executor-py"
    transport: "FDI"
    layer: "module"
    parent: "executor-py"
    machine: "hace-lion-machine"

  - fan_id: "hace-executor-py-racor"
    capabilities:
      - "racor.resolve_target"
      - "racor.resolve_route"
      - "racor.resolve_transport"
    executor: "executor-py"
    transport: "FDI"
    layer: "module"
    parent: "executor-py"
    machine: "hace-lion-machine"
```

## 3. Actor → Executor FAN Binding

```yaml
actor_executor_bindings:
  text-ractor:
    fan_id: "text-ractor"
    executor: "executor-py"
    modules:
      - "hace-executor-py-core"
      - "hace-executor-py-fdi"
      - "hace-executor-py-fpi"
      - "hace-executor-py-capror"
      - "hace-executor-py-racor"
    mode: "mcv"
```

